<section id="mathematical-derivation-km-as-nonparametric-mle" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="mathematical-derivation-km-as-nonparametric-mle">Mathematical Derivation: KM as Nonparametric MLE</h2>
<section id="the-likelihood-function" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-likelihood-function">The Likelihood Function</h3>
<p>Assuming <strong>independent censoring</strong> (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?T%20%5Cperp%20C">), the likelihood for each subject is:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AL(S%20%5Cmid%20%5Ctext%7BData%7D)%20%5Cpropto%20%5Cprod_%7Bi=1%7D%5En%20P(T%20=%20t_i)%5E%7B%5Cdelta_i%7D%20P(T_i%20%3E%20t)%5E%7B1-%5Cdelta_i%7D%0A"></p>
<p>This can be rewritten as: <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AL(S%20%5Cmid%20%5Ctext%7BData%7D)%20=%20%5Cprod_%7Bi=1%7D%5En%20%5C%7BS(t_i%5E-)%20-%20S(t_i)%5C%7D%5E%7B%5Cdelta_i%7D%20S(t_i)%5E%7B1-%5Cdelta_i%7D%0A"></p>
<p>Since all failure mass concentrates on the observed event times <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5C%7Bt_%7B(j)%7D%5C%7D_%7Bj=1%7D%5EJ">, grouping by event times gives:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cboxed%7BL(S%20%5Cmid%20%5Ctext%7BData%7D)%20%5Cpropto%20%5Cprod_%7Bj=1%7D%5EJ%20%5Cbig%5C%7BS(t_%7B(j)%7D%5E-)%20-%20S(t_%7B(j)%7D)%5Cbig%5C%7D%5E%7Bd_j%7D%20%5Ctimes%20S(t_%7B(j)%7D)%5E%7Bc_j%7D%7D%0A"></p>
</section>
<section id="jump-and-survival-ratio" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="jump-and-survival-ratio">Jump and Survival Ratio</h3>
<p>At each <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?t_%7B(j)%7D">, define the <strong>jump</strong>: <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5CDelta%20S_j%20:=%20S(t_%7B(j)%7D%5E-)%20-%20S(t_%7B(j)%7D)%0A"></p>
<p>For a subject at risk at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?t_%7B(j)%7D"> (i.e., <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?T%20%5Cge%20t_%7B(j)%7D">):</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cbegin%7Baligned%7D%0A%5CPr(%5Ctext%7Bfail%20at%20%7D%20t_%7B(j)%7D%20%5Cmid%20%5Ctext%7Bat%20risk%20at%20%7D%20t_%7B(j)%7D)%20&amp;=%20%5Cfrac%7B%5CDelta%20S_j%7D%7BS(t_%7B(j)%7D%5E-)%7D%20=%20%5Clambda_j%20%5C%5C%0A%5CPr(%5Ctext%7Bsurvive%20past%20%7D%20t_%7B(j)%7D%20%5Cmid%20%5Ctext%7Bat%20risk%20at%20%7D%20t_%7B(j)%7D)%20&amp;=%20%5Cfrac%7BS(t_%7B(j)%7D)%7D%7BS(t_%7B(j)%7D%5E-)%7D%20=%201%20-%20%5Clambda_j%0A%5Cend%7Baligned%7D%0A"></p>
</section>
<section id="the-key-ratio-identity" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-key-ratio-identity">The Key Ratio Identity</h3>
<p>For each <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?j">: <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AS(t_%7B(j)%7D)%20=%20(1%20-%20%5Clambda_j)%20S(t_%7B(j)%7D%5E-)%0A"></p>
<p><strong>Reason:</strong> “At risk at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?t_%7B(j)%7D"> and not failing at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?t_%7B(j)%7D">” is exactly “surviving to the next event time <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?t_%7B(j+1)%7D">”.</p>
</section>
<section id="recursion-and-telescoping" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="recursion-and-telescoping">Recursion and Telescoping</h3>
<p>Rearranging gives: <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5CPr(T%20%5Cge%20t_%7B(j+1)%7D)%20=%20%5CPr(T%20%5Cge%20t_%7B(j)%7D)(1%20-%20%5Clambda_j)%0A"></p>
<p>Iterating for <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?l%20=%201,%20%5Cldots,%20j">:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cbegin%7Baligned%7D%0AS(t_%7B(j)%7D%5E-)%20&amp;=%20%5CPr(T%20%5Cge%20t_%7B(j)%7D)%20=%20%5CPr(T%20%5Cge%20t_%7B(1)%7D)%20%5Cprod_%7Bl=1%7D%5E%7Bj-1%7D(1%20-%20%5Clambda_l)%20%5C%5C%0AS(t_%7B(j)%7D)%20&amp;=%20%5CPr(T%20%3E%20t_%7B(j)%7D)%20=%20%5CPr(T%20%5Cge%20t_%7B(1)%7D)%20%5Cprod_%7Bl=1%7D%5Ej%20(1%20-%20%5Clambda_l)%0A%5Cend%7Baligned%7D%0A"></p>
</section>
<section id="product-limit-form" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="product-limit-form">Product-Limit Form</h3>
<p>Without left truncation, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5CPr(T%20%5Cge%20t_%7B(1)%7D)%20=%201">. If <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?t_%7B(j)%7D%20%5Cle%20t%20%3C%20t_%7B(j+1)%7D">:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cboxed%7BS(t)%20=%20%5CPr(T%20%3E%20t)%20=%20%5Cprod_%7Bt_%7B(j)%7D%20%5Cle%20t%7D(1%20-%20%5Clambda_j)%7D%0A"></p>
</section>
<section id="maximizing-the-likelihood" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="maximizing-the-likelihood">Maximizing the Likelihood</h3>
<p>The likelihood can be rewritten as:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cbegin%7Baligned%7D%0AL(S%20%5Cmid%20%5Ctext%7BData%7D)%20&amp;%5Cpropto%20%5Cprod_%7Bj=1%7D%5EJ%20%5Cbig%5C%7BS(t_%7B(j)%7D%5E-)%20-%20S(t_%7B(j)%7D)%5Cbig%5C%7D%5E%7Bd_j%7D%20%5Ctimes%20S(t_%7B(j)%7D)%5E%7Bc_j%7D%20%5C%5C%0A&amp;=%20%5Cprod_%7Bj=1%7D%5EJ%20%5Clambda_j%5E%7Bd_j%7D%20%5Cprod_%7Bk=1%7D%5E%7Bj-1%7D%20(1-%5Clambda_k)%5E%7Bd_j%7D%20%5Ctimes%20%5Cprod_%7Bk=1%7D%5Ej%20(1-%5Clambda_k)%5E%7Bc_j%7D%20%5C%5C%0A&amp;=%20%5Cprod_%7Bj=1%7D%5EJ%20%5Clambda_j%5E%7Bd_j%7D%20(1-%5Clambda_j)%5E%7Bn_j%20-%20d_j%7D%0A%5Cend%7Baligned%7D%0A"></p>
<p>Taking the log-likelihood for each <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Clambda_j">: <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cell_j(%5Clambda_j)%20=%20d_j%20%5Clog%20%5Clambda_j%20+%20(n_j%20-%20d_j)%20%5Clog(1%20-%20%5Clambda_j)%0A"></p>
<p>Setting the derivative to zero: <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cboxed%7B%5Cwidehat%7B%5Clambda%7D_j%20=%20%5Cfrac%7Bd_j%7D%7Bn_j%7D%7D%0A"></p>
<p>Therefore: <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cwidehat%7BS%7D(t)%20=%20%5Cprod_%7Bt_%7B(j)%7D%20%5Cle%20t%7D%20%5Cleft(1%20-%20%5Cfrac%7Bd_j%7D%7Bn_j%7D%5Cright)%0A"></p>
<p>This is the <strong>Kaplan-Meier (product-limit) estimator</strong>, and we have shown it is the <strong>nonparametric maximum likelihood estimator</strong> for the survival function under independent censoring.</p>
</section>
</section>
<section id="summary" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="summary">Summary</h2>
<p>The Kaplan-Meier estimator is:</p>
<ol type="1">
<li><strong>Intuitive</strong>: It multiplies conditional survival probabilities at each event time</li>
<li><strong>Principled</strong>: It is the nonparametric MLE under independent censoring</li>
<li><strong>Practical</strong>: It correctly handles censored observations</li>
<li><strong>Visual</strong>: The step-function plot provides an immediate understanding of survival patterns</li>
</ol>
<p>Understanding the KM estimator is essential for anyone working with time-to-event data in clinical trials, reliability engineering, or any field where survival analysis is applied.</p>


</section>

 ]]></description>
